# Data Analytics Agent Implementation Plan

To eliminate the brittle JSON intent parsing and unlock dynamic, complex queries, we will abstract the SQL generation into an autonomous **Analytics Agent**. When the `supervisor_agent_router` classifies a query as `analytics_agent`, it will hand off execution to this new layer.

## User Review Required
> [!IMPORTANT]
> Please review the architecture of the Analytics Agent below. If you approve, I will construct this new layer and wire it into the main chat route.

## Proposed Changes

### Phase 2: Analytics Agent Layer (Text-to-SQL)

We will build a new python module representing the autonomous Analytics Agent. It will be responsible for translating natural language to SQL, safely executing it, and formulating the final insight.

#### [NEW] [analytics_agent.py](file:///D:/DATATHON/DATATHON/backend/analytics_agent.py)
- **Change:** Create a new module containing the `AnalyticsAgent` class.
- **Methods:**
  - `run(query, history)`: The main orchestration method.
  - `_generate_sql()`: Calls Catalyst GLM with the database schema and conversation history to output a raw SQLite query string.
  - `_execute_sql()`: Connects to `crime.db`. Implements a strict Regex safety check rejecting `DROP`, `DELETE`, `UPDATE`, and `INSERT` keywords. Executes the `SELECT` query and fetches the rows.
  - `_analyze_results()`: Calls Catalyst GLM again, passing the original query and the JSON-stringified SQL results, instructing the model to synthesize a professional natural language response.

